WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.050
Speaker 1: So before giving his completely
deranged CPAC speech, Donald Trump actually

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:09.440
took some questions, and there were actually
some interesting questions asked, and Trump

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.720
was visibly sweaty, disheveled.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:17.130
He seemed confused by many of the questions,
but some of the questions were actually pretty

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.250
interesting.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.510
And this one, it's this this.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:25.730
This one would almost make you blush if Trump
answered it any other way.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:31.739
Trump was asked, as many of you may have heard,
the president of Ukraine has stayed in Ukraine

00:00:31.739 --> 00:00:32.790
and is fighting.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:37.110
He's fighting in Ukraine, trying to repel
the Russian invasion.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:42.150
And Trump was asked If you were in such a
situation, would you also stay and fight?

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.830
And it's like, of course he would.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:45.900
Of course we would.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.500
Trump would be the first guy out.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.830
He'd say, Please evacuate me.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:54.560
And Trump knows he can't say I would be fighting
because no one would believe it.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.530
So even he has to kind of hedge.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:57.530
It's pretty interesting.

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:58.530
Take a look at this one.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:03.430
Speaker 3: And you know, he's not abandoning
his people, are he's saying and taking up

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.489
arms with his countrymen.

00:01:04.489 --> 00:01:08.280
If you were in a similar situation as president,
would you take up arms like Zelensky?

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.399
Speaker 4: Well, you know, you never know
about bravery.

00:01:11.399 --> 00:01:14.950
Some people think they're brave and they're
not brave, and other people don't think of

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:17.520
themselves as very brave and they step up.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.679
You never know until you get tested.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:23.119
Speaker 1: So tricky.

00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:26.009
Even for Trump, it would be too much to say.

00:01:26.009 --> 00:01:28.890
I would be out there with a rifle.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:29.999
Absolutely.

00:01:29.999 --> 00:01:35.249
And so he it's actually he has this moment
where he knows he can't say that.

00:01:35.249 --> 00:01:37.479
Nobody would believe that.

00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:38.799
I think we know the answer.

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:41.360
Trump would not be taking up arms like Zelensky.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:46.100
Trump would be either in the bunker or in
another country altogether.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:51.799
And listen, it's more likely Trump would give
away classified documents if he was in Zelensky's

00:01:51.799 --> 00:01:55.579
position than he would stay and take up arms
and fight anybody.

00:01:55.579 --> 00:01:58.810
Trump was then asked, and this was pretty
interesting.

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:01.100
What would you do differently on Ukraine than
Biden?

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.569
Because Trump saying Biden's doing everything
wrong?

00:02:03.569 --> 00:02:07.859
And Trump says, I guess for security reasons,
he doesn't want to tell you what he would

00:02:07.859 --> 00:02:08.859
do differently.

00:02:08.859 --> 00:02:10.459
Speaker 2: Well, I'll tell you what I would
do things.

00:02:10.459 --> 00:02:15.599
But the last thing I want to do is say it
right now, because if somebody asks me that

00:02:15.599 --> 00:02:20.680
is in a position where they can utilize whatever
it is, I give them, but I certainly wouldn't

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.420
want to be talking about right now.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.010
Speaker 1: It's just not appropriate.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:27.360
And of course, he has no idea of what he would
do differently.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.060
He's just, he says it's Biden's fault, but
this is sort of like he's prepared to release

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:35.510
his health care plan soon, and he's going
to give us the vote evidence of voter fraud

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:36.510
soon.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:37.510
It's all just around the corner.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:42.650
Also, his infrastructure plan, then one oh,
now later in the interview.

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:44.890
And this is in a different moment.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:46.950
Trump is asked about what?

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.140
What about this?

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:52.750
He actually does answer what one thing he
would do, and he says he would get Russia

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:57.310
out of Swift, the swift banking system, which
happened hours before this.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.870
Trump apparently just didn't know that.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:02.459
Speaker 2: Very, very important question to
be asked.

00:03:02.459 --> 00:03:07.200
What is the one sanction or the two sanctions
that have not been implemented to stop Vladimir

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:13.020
Putin that you would implement given a Trump
presence sanctions now you have to just end.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:17.079
Speaker 4: Sanctions are very expensive for
our country also.

00:03:17.079 --> 00:03:20.760
But the one that people are talking about,
which is very, very severe, as you know, is

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:25.510
swift and that just really destroys the banking
system of a country.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:30.870
It's a very big step and we'll see whether
or not that step is taken.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:36.420
But thousands of people, hundreds of thousands
of people could die with this, and this could

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.890
spread to other countries and it could spread
throughout the world.

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:41.310
And this could be a world war.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:42.310
Speaker 1: Yes.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:45.880
OK, so so now Trump changing his tune and
saying this actually could become a world

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:46.880
war.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:49.959
But at the time that he said, the one thing
that that you could look at doing is swift.

00:03:49.959 --> 00:03:54.280
It had been done that it happened hours before
Trump apparently didn't know.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:55.909
So those are the Trump interviews.

00:03:55.909 --> 00:03:56.909
That's the Trump speech.

00:03:56.909 --> 00:03:57.909
It was wacky.

00:03:57.909 --> 00:04:02.329
We'll have some of these clips on our Instagram,
which you can find at David Pakman show.

00:04:02.329 --> 00:05:00.500
And then after the break, we'll look at the
non Trump craziness that happened 

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:07.050
